These are the day-to-day rules for how Team 4 works together. Our mission, goals, and roles are in the [Team Charter](../team-charter.md). If this document and the charter ever disagree, the charter wins.

## Meetings
- Formal meetings are Wednesdays at 7:00 PM before each assignment or checkpoint, and run 15 to 30 minutes.
- If you can't make it, say so in WhatsApp before the meeting starts.
- Every action item leaves the meeting with an owner and a due date. Khumoyun records them in the [Meeting Notes](../meeting-notes.md).

## Communication
- WhatsApp is for quick questions. Loyola Outlook email is for official announcements.
- Reply within 24 hours on weekdays.
- If something could stop you from finishing on time, post it as 🚨 BLOCKER so the team can respond right away.

## Deadlines
- All work is in the repo at least 48 hours before the official due date.
- Those last 48 hours are only for review and fixes, not new work.
- If you think you'll miss a deadline, tell the team as soon as you know.

## GitHub
- Follow the [Documentation Standards](../team/documentation-standards.md) for file names, headers, and formatting.
- Work on a branch and open a pull request. Someone other than the author reviews it before it's merged, using Sohail's review guidelines.
- Commit messages start with a type, like `docs: add risk register`.
- A task is only done when it meets the Definition of Done in the charter.

## AI Use
- Follow the [AI Policy](../ai/ai-policy.md).
- Log any AI help in the [AI Use Log](../ai/ai-use-log.md) and mention it in your pull request.

## Disagreements
1. Talk to the person directly first.
2. If that doesn't fix it, bring it to Victoria.
3. If it's still stuck, the team votes at the next meeting.
4. If someone keeps not contributing, we go to the instructor.

Important decisions that come out of this get recorded in the [Decision Log](../decisions/decision-log.md).
